That's how I always accessed it.

2039
01:26:22.730 --> 01:26:24.940
I would go to Thailand and then get

2040
01:26:24.940 --> 01:26:26.850
into the ethnic provinces from there,

2041
01:26:26.850 --> 01:26:28.230
which a lot of journalists do.

2042
01:26:28.230 --> 01:26:29.683
And you can do it legally.

2043
01:26:30.940 --> 01:26:32.640
So we'll see.

2044
01:26:32.640 --> 01:26:35.280
There's already refugee camps on the Thailand border

2045
01:26:35.280 --> 01:26:37.680
that have stood for 20, 30 years.

2046
01:26:37.680 --> 01:26:39.830
But people have left them and gone back

2047
01:26:39.830 --> 01:26:42.930
and started businesses and done well.

2048
01:26:42.930 --> 01:26:45.280
But now, it's all coming back around.

2049
01:26:45.280 --> 01:26:47.620
And those same villages that people went back to

2050
01:26:47.620 --> 01:26:49.810
are getting overrun by military again now.

2051
01:26:49.810 --> 01:26:51.950
All right, well, we'll keep an eye on this.

2052
01:26:51.950 --> 01:26:54.823
Yeah, sorry, I feel like I'm talking too loud.

2053
01:26:55.660 --> 01:26:56.980
I think you're all right.
Okay.

2054
01:26:56.980 --> 01:26:58.890
Jason will modulate you.

2055
01:26:58.890 --> 01:27:00.640
You'll end up sounding like butter.

2056
01:27:01.950 --> 01:27:03.450
Let's do some listener questions.

2057
01:27:03.450 --> 01:27:04.370
Let's do it.
Hey guys,

2058
01:27:04.370 --> 01:27:05.890
this is will from Portland, Oregon.

2059
01:27:05.890 --> 01:27:06.793
I had a question.

2060
01:27:07.720 --> 01:27:09.470
I was a vegan for awhile.

2061
01:27:09.470 --> 01:27:12.030
I was inspired by Rich when he first started the podcast.

2062
01:27:12.030 --> 01:27:14.990
I read your memoir and all that.

2063
01:27:14.990 --> 01:27:19.990
And did my first marathon about seven years ago.

2064
01:27:22.407 --> 01:27:24.350
Shortly after that, my father passed away,

2065
01:27:24.350 --> 01:27:28.943
and as life happens, you kind of just lose all motivation

2066
01:27:28.943 --> 01:27:32.120
and I stopped being vegan, stopped running completely.

2067
01:27:32.120 --> 01:27:35.720
And I'm a lot heavier than I used to be.

2068
01:27:35.720 --> 01:27:38.790
And I just wanted to know for heavier folks

2069
01:27:38.790 --> 01:27:41.123
who are trying to get back into the game or just start it,

2070
01:27:41.123 --> 01:27:44.653
there's not a lot of information out there of how to do it.

2071
01:27:45.940 --> 01:27:48.370
It's hard to ego check yourself

2072
01:27:48.370 --> 01:27:50.710
and know that you can't do what you once used to do.

2073
01:27:50.710 --> 01:27:53.320
I just wanted to know if you guys had any advice

2074
01:27:53.320 --> 01:27:58.320
on starting over for folks who have kind of lost it all

2075
01:27:58.360 --> 01:28:01.950
and are trying to grasp the reality

2076
01:28:01.950 --> 01:28:04.240
of where we're at and where we once were

2077
01:28:04.240 --> 01:28:08.310
and just the mind game that that plays sometimes.

2078
01:28:08.310 --> 01:28:09.250
Thank you guys so much.

2079
01:28:09.250 --> 01:28:12.213
I love listening to you guys, big fan, bye.

2080
01:28:14.330 --> 01:28:15.980
Thanks for your question, Will.

2081
01:28:18.632 --> 01:28:19.465
That's a good question.

2082
01:28:19.465 --> 01:28:22.580
I think it's a question that a lot of people can relate to.

2083
01:28:22.580 --> 01:28:24.310
And I have a few thoughts on this.

2084
01:28:24.310 --> 01:28:26.730
I mean, first of all, the only day better

2085
01:28:26.730 --> 01:28:31.010
than yesterday to begin something like this is today, right?

2086
01:28:31.010 --> 01:28:33.820
And the good news is, you've done it before.

2087
01:28:33.820 --> 01:28:37.360
So you actually already know what to do.

2088
01:28:37.360 --> 01:28:39.490
You mentioned that there's not a lot

2089
01:28:39.490 --> 01:28:41.813
of information out there on how to do it.

2090
01:28:42.730 --> 01:28:43.600
I disagree.

2091
01:28:43.600 --> 01:28:45.420
I think there's plenty of information.

2092
01:28:45.420 --> 01:28:49.350
I don't think that we're thirsting

2093
01:28:49.350 --> 01:28:51.890
for information that doesn't exist

2094
01:28:51.890 --> 01:28:56.890
on how to make this kind of transformation.

2095
01:28:56.990 --> 01:29:01.120
So information, in my opinion, you did this before,

2096
01:29:01.120 --> 01:29:03.190
you read my book, you went vegan, you ran a marathon.

2097
01:29:03.190 --> 01:29:05.450
Like information is not your malfunction.

2098
01:29:05.450 --> 01:29:08.120
Action is your problem.

2099
01:29:08.120 --> 01:29:10.550
And I think that you're a victim

2100
01:29:10.550 --> 01:29:13.920
of your own kind of shame at the moment.

2101
01:29:13.920 --> 01:29:17.190
So my suggestion is to find a way to bury that shame spiral

2102
01:29:17.190 --> 01:29:21.070
and to put an end to the pity party and just begin

2103
01:29:21.070 --> 01:29:24.590
by putting one foot in front of the other.

2104
01:29:24.590 --> 01:29:27.160
What is right in front of you to do right now?

2105
01:29:27.160 --> 01:29:29.410
Can you go out the door and go for a walk?

2106
01:29:29.410 --> 01:29:30.960
What is your next meal gonna be?

2107
01:29:30.960 --> 01:29:34.020
And I think with that, with those tiny steps,

2108
01:29:34.020 --> 01:29:36.350
you start to create a little bit of momentum.

2109
01:29:36.350 --> 01:29:39.630
And there's huge power in momentum.

2110
01:29:39.630 --> 01:29:43.220
If you can create just the tiniest positive change

2111
01:29:43.220 --> 01:29:46.240
that's a little bit different from your daily MO,

2112
01:29:46.240 --> 01:29:47.720
that will help free you

2113
01:29:47.720 --> 01:29:50.800
from this position that you're in right now,

2114
01:29:50.800 --> 01:29:54.160
which is being stuck in a negative cycle.

2115
01:29:54.160 --> 01:29:59.160
So the focus should be on, what can you do right now?

2116
01:30:00.770 --> 01:30:02.090
You can't run a marathon.

2117
01:30:02.090 --> 01:30:03.820
You haven't been vegan for a while.

2118
01:30:03.820 --> 01:30:05.630
You put on a bunch of weight.

2119
01:30:05.630 --> 01:30:08.110
You can go for a walk, you can eat a salad,

2120
01:30:08.110 --> 01:30:11.940
and you can celebrate those tiny wins

2121
01:30:11.940 --> 01:30:15.300
until you slowly get more emotionally

2122
01:30:15.300 --> 01:30:19.260
connected to this arc of improvement.

2123
01:30:19.260 --> 01:30:22.220
And with that, the path will present itself.

2124
01:30:22.220 --> 01:30:25.380
You don't need somebody to deliver you

2125
01:30:25.380 --> 01:30:29.130
an information packet with your plan for the next two years.

2126
01:30:29.130 --> 01:30:32.510
What you need to do is to take action.

2127
01:30:32.510 --> 01:30:36.380
And I think, at odds with that right now,

2128
01:30:36.380 --> 01:30:38.500
this enemy that you're facing

2129
01:30:38.500 --> 01:30:41.860
is comparing yourself to this person

2130
01:30:41.860 --> 01:30:44.260
that you were seven years ago.

2131
01:30:44.260 --> 01:30:46.510
Comparison is the thief of joy.

2132
01:30:46.510 --> 01:30:47.850
So stop comparing yourself

2133
01:30:47.850 --> 01:30:50.340
to your past self or to other people.

2134
01:30:50.340 --> 01:30:53.060
It's this idea of not training

2135
01:30:53.060 --> 01:30:54.290
where you think you should be.

2136
01:30:54.290 --> 01:30:55.660
Like, if you go out for a jog

2137
01:30:55.660 --> 01:30:57.050
and you get tired after a block

2138
01:30:57.050 --> 01:30:58.510
and you feel like you have to walk,

2139
01:30:58.510 --> 01:30:59.840
and then you're beating yourself up

2140
01:30:59.840 --> 01:31:01.650
because I used to run a marathon,

2141
01:31:01.650 --> 01:31:03.740
and look at how much weight I put on.

2142
01:31:03.740 --> 01:31:05.030
It's not about that.

2143
01:31:05.030 --> 01:31:07.080
It's not about training where you think you should be.

2144
01:31:07.080 --> 01:31:11.190
It's about accepting and embracing where you are right now

2145
01:31:11.190 --> 01:31:13.943
and doing what you are capable of doing,

2146
01:31:13.943 --> 01:31:15.380
because that's the only way

2147
01:31:15.380 --> 01:31:18.840
that you get anything done or make any progress.

2148
01:31:18.840 --> 01:31:21.900
So you have everything you need.

2149
01:31:21.900 --> 01:31:26.797
And I think you need to disabuse yourself of this idea

2150
01:31:27.640 --> 01:31:30.890
that you're gonna stay in your status quo

2151
01:31:30.890 --> 01:31:34.490
until you experience some windfall of motivation.

2152
01:31:34.490 --> 01:31:36.140
Like you're waiting to be motivated.

2153
01:31:36.140 --> 01:31:38.520
Like you've said, I just don't feel motivated,

2154
01:31:38.520 --> 01:31:40.380
I don't have any motivation.

2155
01:31:40.380 --> 01:31:43.010
And I think when you're in that mindset,

2156
01:31:43.010 --> 01:31:45.470
you're waiting to feel motivated to do something.

2157
01:31:45.470 --> 01:31:48.490
And that's not how it works.

2158
01:31:48.490 --> 01:31:50.560
That's in fact, a trap.

2159
01:31:50.560 --> 01:31:52.830
You don't need to be motivated to make change.

2160
01:31:52.830 --> 01:31:54.390
You just need to do.

2161
01:31:54.390 --> 01:31:56.803
Mood follows action, which is what I always say.

2162
01:31:57.719 --> 01:32:02.719
So a day at a time, just like they say in 12 step.

2163
01:32:03.510 --> 01:32:04.810
What can you do today?

2164
01:32:04.810 --> 01:32:06.150
Can you eat a little bit better?

2165
01:32:06.150 --> 01:32:09.130
Can you move your body in a way that you didn't yesterday?

2166
01:32:09.130 --> 01:32:11.530
Can your head hit the pillow

2167
01:32:11.530 --> 01:32:13.270
with a little bit more self-esteem

2168
01:32:13.270 --> 01:32:15.330
because you exercise some self-care

2169
01:32:15.330 --> 01:32:18.450
and some self-love by moving the needle

2170
01:32:18.450 --> 01:32:20.410
ever so slightly in the right direction?

2171
01:32:20.410 --> 01:32:23.310
And when you start to string some days together

2172
01:32:23.310 --> 01:32:26.760
of doing just that, it doesn't take long

2173
01:32:26.760 --> 01:32:29.360
before you wake up a little bit more excited

2174
01:32:29.360 --> 01:32:31.480
for that walk that turns into a jog

2175
01:32:31.480 --> 01:32:34.470
that eventually over time will turn into a run

2176
01:32:34.470 --> 01:32:36.530
and just might bring you back

2177
01:32:36.530 --> 01:32:39.380
to the starting line of another marathon.

2178
01:32:39.380 --> 01:32:40.213
I love it.

2179
01:32:41.230 --> 01:32:45.160
It reminds me of like, baseball season's around the corner.

2180
01:32:45.160 --> 01:32:47.830
It reminds me of like those hitters that are in a slump.

2181
01:32:47.830 --> 01:32:49.890
What do they do is they just focus

2182
01:32:49.890 --> 01:32:51.360
on their approach to each at-bat,

2183
01:32:51.360 --> 01:32:53.160
because you can't control getting a hit,

2184
01:32:53.160 --> 01:32:54.360
'cause there's so many bad bounces

2185
01:32:54.360 --> 01:32:57.102
or the way the ball, you just don't know.

2186
01:32:57.102 --> 01:32:59.540
The balls and strikes are called differently every day.

2187
01:32:59.540 --> 01:33:02.130
But can you change your approach to each at-bat

2188
01:33:02.130 --> 01:33:04.260
and then start stringing some good ones together?

2189
01:33:04.260 --> 01:33:06.210
And sort of then eventually you start seeing

2190
01:33:06.210 --> 01:33:07.967
a couple of hits and the momentum turns

2191
01:33:07.967 --> 01:33:09.100
and your confidence turn.

2192
01:33:09.100 --> 01:33:11.020
Yeah, I mean, I just can't stress

2193
01:33:11.020 --> 01:33:13.110
the importance of tiny little actions.

2194
01:33:13.110 --> 01:33:16.690
Like if Will's running shoes are in the closet,

2195
01:33:16.690 --> 01:33:19.130
pull them out of the closet and put them in the hallway.

2196
01:33:19.130 --> 01:33:20.390
Like, if all you did was that,

2197
01:33:20.390 --> 01:33:22.780
well, that's more than you did yesterday.

2198
01:33:22.780 --> 01:33:24.910
Next time, put them next to your bed.

2199
01:33:24.910 --> 01:33:26.540
The next day, like, why don't you put them on

2200
01:33:26.540 --> 01:33:27.880
when you sit up in the morning,

2201
01:33:27.880 --> 01:33:29.930
and like, walk to your front door?

2202
01:33:29.930 --> 01:33:32.590
Like, what can you do?

2203
01:33:32.590 --> 01:33:34.330
And then do those tiny things

2204
01:33:34.330 --> 01:33:36.600
that are very digestible and doable,

2205
01:33:36.600 --> 01:33:39.733
count them as wins and build on that momentum.

2206
01:33:40.920 --> 01:33:42.110
That's a great advice.

2207
01:33:42.110 --> 01:33:44.070
And the fact that you're listening, Will,

2208
01:33:44.070 --> 01:33:45.070
shows that you're still,

2209
01:33:45.070 --> 01:33:46.270
your head's still in the game.

2210
01:33:46.270 --> 01:33:47.103
Of course.

2211
01:33:49.510 --> 01:33:50.770
All right.

2212
01:33:50.770 --> 01:33:52.670
We're going to Europe for this one.

2213
01:33:52.670 --> 01:33:53.840
Hey Rich and Adam.

2214
01:33:53.840 --> 01:33:56.130
This is Tanya from Lucerne, Switzerland.

2215
01:33:56.130 --> 01:33:58.720
I would love to hear your thoughts on this topic.

2216
01:33:58.720 --> 01:34:01.900
So I've been living plant-based for over five years.

2217
01:34:01.900 --> 01:34:04.050
I try to mostly buy things secondhand.

2218
01:34:04.050 --> 01:34:05.860
I always stop to question

2219
01:34:05.860 --> 01:34:08.550
if what I wanna buy is something that I really need.

2220
01:34:08.550 --> 01:34:10.650
And I do this partly because I'm really concerned

2221
01:34:10.650 --> 01:34:12.780
for our planet's future and its resources,

2222
01:34:12.780 --> 01:34:15.660
but also because I have a one-year-old kid

2223
01:34:15.660 --> 01:34:17.830
and I really want him to grow up living consciously

2224
01:34:17.830 --> 01:34:20.100
and making deliberate choices.

2225
01:34:20.100 --> 01:34:22.820
So I try really hard to remind myself

2226
01:34:22.820 --> 01:34:25.560
that I'm in control only of myself.

2227
01:34:25.560 --> 01:34:28.930
I often struggle with older people from other generations

2228
01:34:28.930 --> 01:34:33.350
who live very frivolously with like seemingly little concern

2229
01:34:33.350 --> 01:34:36.500
about the impact they're having on the planet.

2230
01:34:36.500 --> 01:34:38.580
I know that grandparents can have

2231
01:34:38.580 --> 01:34:41.070
a massive influence on their grandchildren.

2232
01:34:41.070 --> 01:34:44.490
So have you found good talking points to address this?

2233
01:34:44.490 --> 01:34:47.680
Or do you just try to not think about it too much

2234
01:34:47.680 --> 01:34:49.840
and let people live how they want to?

2235
01:34:49.840 --> 01:34:51.270
Thanks so much.

2236
01:34:51.270 --> 01:34:54.280
Tanya from Lucerne.
Yes, Lucerne in the house.

2237
01:34:54.280 --> 01:34:56.140
Isn't that where they make the butter?

2238
01:34:56.140 --> 01:34:57.250
Is that where they make the butter?

2239
01:34:57.250 --> 01:34:58.083
Is it?

2240
01:34:58.083 --> 01:34:59.373
Shout out Lucerne.
I think so.

2241
01:35:00.880 --> 01:35:03.030
Thanks for your question.

2242
01:35:03.030 --> 01:35:04.003
This is tricky.

2243
01:35:06.360 --> 01:35:09.640
I think it's important to, of course,

2244
01:35:09.640 --> 01:35:10.770
make the best choices

2245
01:35:10.770 --> 01:35:12.900
that are in alignment with your values.

2246
01:35:12.900 --> 01:35:14.160
And that's what Tanya's doing.

2247
01:35:14.160 --> 01:35:17.670
She's conscientious about her needs and her wants

2248
01:35:17.670 --> 01:35:22.060
and tries to make sure that her consumer choices

2249
01:35:22.060 --> 01:35:24.040
are in alignment with her values

2250
01:35:24.040 --> 01:35:26.030
and that's something to be celebrated.

2251
01:35:26.030 --> 01:35:30.610
And certainly, that's healthy modeling for your child,

2252
01:35:30.610 --> 01:35:32.060
because it's not about what you say,

2253
01:35:32.060 --> 01:35:37.060
it's about what you do, it's about your behavior.

2254
01:35:37.120 --> 01:35:39.290
But I also think this question has a lot to do

2255
01:35:39.290 --> 01:35:41.070
with controlling the controllables.

2256
01:35:41.070 --> 01:35:42.377
Understanding what you can control

2257
01:35:42.377 --> 01:35:43.740
and what you can't control,

2258
01:35:43.740 --> 01:35:46.930
and really having a healthy mindset

2259
01:35:46.930 --> 01:35:49.810
around how you calibrate all of that.

2260
01:35:49.810 --> 01:35:52.220
As a parent, you lead by example in action.

2261
01:35:52.220 --> 01:35:55.170
Again, you model this behavior for your kids.

2262
01:35:55.170 --> 01:35:59.330
But it's also important to not be a martyr,

2263
01:35:59.330 --> 01:36:01.850
especially if you're, if part of your interest

2264
01:36:01.850 --> 01:36:04.450
is in trying to inspire the next generation.

2265
01:36:04.450 --> 01:36:07.140
If you're suffering, then that doesn't become

2266
01:36:07.140 --> 01:36:09.610
an aspirational way to live your life.

2267
01:36:09.610 --> 01:36:13.120
And ultimately, that's gonna set you up

2268
01:36:13.120 --> 01:36:14.640
for your kid to just rebel,

2269
01:36:14.640 --> 01:36:17.070
saying I don't wanna live my life like that.

2270
01:36:17.070 --> 01:36:18.890
That doesn't look like any fun.

2271
01:36:18.890 --> 01:36:19.850
I wanna thrive.

2272
01:36:19.850 --> 01:36:22.460
And why was I deprived of all these things?

2273
01:36:22.460 --> 01:36:24.150
I'm gonna go out into the world and get them.

2274
01:36:24.150 --> 01:36:27.737
Like kids are always going to differentiate in that way.

2275
01:36:27.737 --> 01:36:31.030
And they're gonna wanna explore the opposite

2276
01:36:31.030 --> 01:36:32.660
of what they've been presented with.

2277
01:36:32.660 --> 01:36:36.110
So you have to be mindful about that a little bit.

2278
01:36:36.110 --> 01:36:39.030
And I think it's important to not overly in an unhealthy way

2279
01:36:39.030 --> 01:36:42.680
attach to how your child's moral compass will evolve.

2280
01:36:42.680 --> 01:36:44.950
And I say that as a parent of four,

2281
01:36:44.950 --> 01:36:46.890
and two teenagers right now,

2282
01:36:46.890 --> 01:36:50.390
like I've experienced a variety of permutations on this.

2283
01:36:50.390 --> 01:36:54.250
Everything from we love the way that you parented us

2284
01:36:54.250 --> 01:36:56.800
and we wanna model our own value system

2285
01:36:56.800 --> 01:36:59.100
based upon how we were raised to,

2286
01:36:59.100 --> 01:37:01.450
I don't want anything to do with this.

2287
01:37:01.450 --> 01:37:03.067
Keep that, get that vegan butter out of here.

2288
01:37:03.067 --> 01:37:05.300
And a lot of that just has to do

2289
01:37:05.300 --> 01:37:07.000
with how they come out of the womb.

2290
01:37:07.000 --> 01:37:08.470
You know what I mean?

2291
01:37:08.470 --> 01:37:10.800
But my point being that-
The ultimate blockchain.

2292
01:37:10.800 --> 01:37:13.310
You only have so much control over these things.

